  "body": "Decision record for issue #5905 (task 14150) — the provider security model, settling the questions #5900 §6 expressly left to this record.\n\n## What it decides\n\n- **Identity (D1):** a provider is its keypair in the ID object model; everything binds to the provider instance (identity, instance, manifest version) that #5900 D1 already grants against. Names are display/routing labels, never authority.\n- **Authenticity & admission (D2):** manifests are signed and verified at admission and on every change; admission is an explicit admin registry act; every class enters at `default_ceiling: excluded` (F13.7's client rule generalised); manifest widening re-runs admission and old grants refuse at use.\n- **Impersonation (D3):** addressing binds keys, never names/addresses; a registry name collision under a different key is a journaled refusal, never a rebind.\n- **Rogue providers (D4):** blast radius is structural (ceiling ∩ grant, bounds, classes, per-use S3 approval); removal ladder ceiling → registry → revocation, none needing the provider's cooperation; observation dishonesty named honestly as the residual risk, with attribution guaranteed.\n- **Bridge compromise (D5):** bridges/brokers are transport, never principals — no grants, no ceilings; compromise yields drop/delay/replay only, and replay never re-executes.\n- **Capability confusion (D6):** capability identity is the tuple (provider identity, capability id, manifest version); renames/re-classes mint new tuples old grants don't follow.\n- **Ceiling-composition audit (D7):** effective authority must be enumerable from registry + grant ledger + journal alone, with named standing audit flags.\n\n## Boundaries kept\n\nNo parent decision is changed: #5686's model, #5900's grant shape/classes/§5 invariants, #5903's embedded instantiations, and #5904's offline semantics are taken as given in §1, with an explicit conflicts check. Server/world ceiling-before-grant behaviour is preserved verbatim (task acceptance). #5931 consumed as survey input; #5898/#5899 scopes untouched.\n\nImplementation is filed as #7944 (admission signature verification, default-excluded admission, manifest-change re-admission, D7 audit enumeration), so the design does not sit without a tracked next action.\n\nDocs-only change, following the sibling decision-record format of #5900/#5904.\n\n🤖 Queue worker lane code-u, task 14150.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796789159&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7946&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7946&signature=29ba57a634e6e163e2cbddf3d8e7fb31c955b9aa7a6d83a10241ea17d99f3356\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7946?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
